{number: 47}
{title: Blessed Assurance, Jesus Is Mine}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[D] Blessed assurance, [G] Jesus is [D] mine!
O what a [Bm] foretaste of [E7] glory di-[A] vine!
[D] Heir of salvation, [G] purchase of [D] God,
Born of His [Em] Spirit, [A7] washed in His [D] blood.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
This is my [D] story, this is my [G] song,
Praising my [D] Savior [Bm] all the day [A] long;
This is my [D] story, this is my [G] song,
Praising my [D] Savior [A7] all the day [D] long.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[D] Perfect submission, [G] perfect de-[D] light,
Visions of [Bm] rapture now [E7] burst on my [A] sight;
[D] Angels descending, [G] bring from a-[D] bove
Echoes of [Em] mercy, [A7] whispers of [D] love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[D] Perfect submission, [G] all is at [D] rest,
I in my [Bm] Savior am [E7] happy and [A] blest;
[D] Watching and waiting, [G] looking a-[D] bove,
Filled with His [Em] goodness, [A7] lost in His [D] love.
{end_of_verse}
